-----------------------------------------------------------------------------


                          System checkup list
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The preferences file for the system/bbs must be in your S: directory.


Following directories must be present in your bbs path.

ACCESSLEVEL    : this directory is where the system will look
                 for accesslevel files, called LEVEL_xxx
                 where xxx is a number.

CONFS          : path to all conferences available


DEF_BBSTEXT    : path to default texts.
                 such as login.txt,logoff.txt,menu.txt

FCHECK         : when a file is uploaded, the filechecker will
                 look in this directory for a matching extension.
                 and execute the filechecker for this fileextension.


NODEx          : NODE path.
                 subpath to all files related to each node.
                 such as NOCALLERSAT, login.txt,logoff.txt.. etc..


USERTYPE       : this directory holds all usertype configurations available
                 to sysop....


COMMANDS       : This directory is the path to external commands
                 used by the system, and online users.

                 BBSCmd           :subdirectory to bbs commands

                 SysCmd           :subdirectory to system commands


PRESETS        : Directory holds preset information files.
                 Files are called :  PRESET_x


SYSTEM         : This directory holds system files.
                 Such as logs and other system related files.


USERS          : In this directory all users are placed.


BULLETINS      : This is the default directory for bulletins
                 viewed by a user using the B command.


BULL           : this directory is where default BULL texts
                 will be put.


Following files must be available in your bbs path.

LogicBBS       :
LogicBBS.info  : These 2 files are the main program and its icon.


UserList.bbs   : This file is created by the system.
                 and hold names of users on the bbs
                 Only used in combination with useraccount locating
                 by number.

Conf.Cfg       : this file is the conference configuration file.

nuttons.def    : buttons/nuttons config file.
